  <div id="sutta">
  
    <h4 id="thig1.17" class="h1">Thig 1:17  Dhammā</h4>
          <div class="verse">
            <p>Wandering for alms—</p>
            <p>weak, leaning on a staff,<span class="fn"><a href="#thig1.17note01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--></p>
            <p>with trembling limbs—</p>
            <p>I fell down right there on the ground.</p>
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>Seeing the drawbacks of the body,</p>
              <p>my mind was then</p>
              <p class="v6">set free.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
          </div><!--end verse-->
          <div class="note">
            <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
            <p id="thig1.17note01">1. Reading <em>daṇḍamolubbha</em> with the Burmese, Sinhalese, and PTS editions. The Thai edition has <em>daṇḍamādāya,</em> “holding a staff.”</p>
          </div><!--end notes-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
